// AuthFederatedWithBody Exchange a note from a registered outside issuer for a session
//
// Off unless FEDERATED_IDENTITY_ENABLED is true, and a 404 while it is off. The note is a short-lived JWT signed with Ed25519 by a key an operator registered for that issuer; the reply is the same pair POST /auth/login returns, so a client handles the session the same way afterwards. A note works exactly once. The account is found by the (issuer, subject) pair and not by the address in the note, so an issuer cannot name an existing account and be handed it; the first note for a subject creates an account, and its role comes from the operator's own map of group claims, never from the note alone. Every verification failure is the same 401 with the same message, on purpose: the reason is in the server log, where an integrator can be shown it and a forger cannot read it.
