	// The password works again as it was. The API keys do not come back, since deactivating deleted them, and neither does the calendar feed URL: deactivating rotated it, so the person fetches the new one. If the old password should not work again, a reset-password afterwards issues a new one. Calling it on an active account changes nothing. A UNIT_ADMIN has the same limits as for deactivating.
	//
	// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /api/v1/users/{user_id}/reactivate (the `UsersReactivate` operationId).
